{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Or a young pigeon or a turtledove</b> — In all places the Masorah puts turtledoves before young pigeons, except here, because she brings only one. For if she finds a pigeon, she does not take a turtledove, because its mate mourns over it and does not pair with another."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:13.596860449Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}